        <tr><td>Backups</td><td>Backups are kept for up to 12 months and then deleted (nightly backups are overwritten within the month; monthly snapshots and backups taken before maintenance work are kept longer). Data you delete may persist in backups until they expire.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table></div>
  </section>

  <section id="choices">
    <h2>10. Your choices and rights</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Edit or delete your posts and comments, and choose which profile panels are public, at any time.</li>
      <li>In Camfrog rooms, <code>!incognito</code> / <code>!bridge hide</code> keep your name off the website. Incognito does more than that: see <a href="#incognito">Incognito</a> below.</li>
      <li>Choose who can see your cam on the website, or switch it off: see <a href="#livecams">Live cams</a>.</li>
      <li><b>Make Pepe forget you</b> and delete your private conversations with him: see <a href="#forget">below</a>.</li>
      <li><b>Download your data</b> or <b>delete your account</b> in <a href="/settings/account">Settings → Account</a>. A deleted account is closed after a 14-day grace period in which signing in cancels it; Pepe also forgets your Camfrog name.</li>
      <li>Turn inbox notices on or off in your inbox settings; choose who can message you, block people and turn Camfrog alerts for messages on or off in your message settings.</li>
      <li>Clear cookies and local storage in your browser (you'll be signed out).</li>
      <li>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, delete or export your personal data, to object to or restrict some processing, and to complain to your data-protection authority. Email <a href="mailto:privacy@publicaccess.tv">privacy@publicaccess.tv</a> from the address on your account and we'll respond within the time the law requires. We may need to keep some data (for example safety records about content that was reported) where the law allows or requires.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3 id="incognito">Incognito</h3>
    <p>Incognito is a switch for your chat identity (your linked Camfrog name). It is off unless you turn it on. Turn it on or off with <code>!incognito on</code> / <code>!incognito off</code> in chat (in a room or a PM to Pepe), or in <a href="/settings/privacy">Settings → Privacy</a> on the website. Both change the same setting, and you get an inbox notice when it changes.</p>
    <p>While incognito is on:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Pepe doesn't remember anything new you say</b> - in rooms, in PMs, in direct messages on the site or on Telegram. Lines that were still waiting to be remembered when you switched it on are discarded.</li>
      <li><b>You're "someone" on the website:</b> your name is hidden on the live room view and your chat lines aren't shown there, so they can't be quoted or turn up as mentions.</li>
      <li><b>Captures of you are private:</b> snaps and clips that show you can't be kept or posted, your cam can't be used as a reference for AI pictures, and Pepe doesn't keep your mic audio for clips.</li>
      <li><b>You're left out of bounty evidence and analytics:</b> your lines are never quoted or sent to the AI judge when a bounty is checked, your most-used words aren't recorded for your profile analytics, and room statistics count you without naming you.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><b>What it doesn't do:</b> it only stops <i>new</i> data. It doesn't delete what Pepe or the site already stored about you, including memories, chat logs, captures and analytics from before you switched it on. To delete Pepe's memories and your private conversations with him, use <a href="#forget">Make Pepe forget me</a>; for everything else, or to get a copy, use Settings → Account or email <a href="mailto:privacy@publicaccess.tv">privacy@publicaccess.tv</a> from the address on your account (see your rights above). Your points, games and commands work as usual while it's on.</p>
    <h3 id="forget">Make Pepe forget me</h3>
    <p>In <a href="/settings/privacy#forget">Settings → Privacy</a>, or with <code>!forgetme now</code> and then <code>!forgetme confirm</code> in Camfrog, you can make Pepe forget you. It deletes, and can't be undone:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>everything Pepe remembers about you: what he learned, your nicknames and linked names, and your mic history;</li>
      <li>your private conversations with him: Camfrog private messages, "Message Pepe" on the website (for both sides of the conversation) and the Telegram chat.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>It doesn't delete what you said in public rooms (chat, mic transcripts, snaps and clips), because that's the room's record and involves other people, and it doesn't switch on incognito, so Pepe starts learning again if you keep talking to him. We keep a record that you asked (when, and how many messages were deleted), never what was said. Deleted data may persist in backups until they expire (see section 9).</p>
  </section>

  <section id="children">
    <h2>11. Children</h2>
    <p>PATV is for adults (18+). We don't knowingly collect data from anyone under 18; if we learn we have, we close the account and delete the data, except where we must keep it to report abuse.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="security">
    <h2>12. Security</h2>
    <p>Passwords are hashed, the site is served over HTTPS, sign-in cookies can't be read by page scripts, the most sensitive data is limited to administrators with every view logged, and identity keys are stored as salted hashes. No system is perfectly secure; if a breach affects you we'll tell you as the law requires.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="transfers">
    <h2>13. Where data is stored</h2>
    <p>Our servers are in the United States, and service providers such as Cloudflare may process data in other countries. Where the law requires, we use appropriate safeguards for these transfers.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="changes">
    <h2>14. Changes</h2>
    <p>We'll update this policy when what we do changes. The "Last updated" date at the top shows the latest version; for significant changes we'll also give notice on the site.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><b>19 October 2026:</b> added <a href="#pepe-photos">Photos you send Pepe</a> (section 6): an AI model looks at them so he can answer, on our own hardware unless an administrator switches on an outside provider (the conversation says which); the adult-content check and what is kept for the administrators when it suggests a minor (the check's scores and a blurred thumbnail, only while the automatic picture checks are on for messages); that he keeps neither the photo nor a memory of it; and that his reply stays in the conversation, where his later answers (which may come from an outside provider) can read it.</li>
      <li><b>18 October 2026:</b> added <a href="#browser-notifications">Browser notifications</a> (section 2): opt-in per browser, what is stored, that a notification never carries what was said or who said it, and the push services that pass it on (section 7). New rows in sections 8 and 9.</li>
      <li><b>15 October 2026:</b> added <a href="#livecams">Live cams</a> (section 3): who can watch your cam on the website (verified members by default), asking and answering, blocks, being told who watched, PATV staff moderation views ("ghost mode", logged), and Pepe's main stream; <a href="#forget">Make Pepe forget me</a> (section 10); downloading your data and deleting your account; and that PATV asks search engines and AI crawlers not to index it (section 6). New retention rows in section 9.</li>
      <li><b>13 October 2026:</b> added <a href="#incognito">Incognito</a> (section 10): what the incognito switch stops, what it doesn't delete, and that it can now be changed in Settings → Privacy as well as with <code>!incognito</code>. A clarification of a setting you control; nothing about what we collect changed.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

